\import{fcap-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fcap}
\tag{spin}
\tag{clifford}

\taxon{Lemma}
\title{Opposite Lorentz signatures share an even-algebra action dictionary}

\p{Keep the Pauli convention of \ref{fcap-002L}:
#{Q_{1,3}(v)=t^2-x_1^2-x_2^2-x_3^2}, #{A_j=e_0e_j}, and
#{\Psi(A_j)=\sigma_j}. For
#{Q_{3,1}(y)=y_0^2+y_1^2+y_2^2-y_3^2}, write #{f_0,\ldots,f_3}
for the coordinate generators. The real linear bijection

##{T(t,x_1,x_2,x_3)=(-x_2,x_1,-x_3,t)}

satisfies #{Q_{3,1}(Tv)=-Q_{1,3}(v)}. There is a real algebra equivalence

##{E:\Cl^+(Q_{1,3})\longrightarrow\Cl^+(Q_{3,1}),
\qquad E(vw)=-T(v)T(w).}

It preserves reversion and restricts to an equivalence of the actual
Spin groups. Their vector actions satisfy

##{T(svs^{-1})=E(s)T(v)E(s)^{-1}.}}

\p{For the construction, complexify and send #{v\mapsto iT(v)}.
Its square is #{Q_{1,3}(v)}, so the Clifford universal property gives an
algebra map. On an even word of length #{2k} its value is
#{(-1)^kT(v_1)\cdots T(v_{2k})}, which is real. This defines #{E} by
scalar extension as in \ref{fcap-003V}. The reverse construction sends
#{w\mapsto iT^{-1}(w)}; the two composites negate generators and
therefore fix every even word. Reversing an even word commutes with
#{E}. The dimension-four carrier lemma \ref{fcap-002J} now identifies
the reverse-norm-one even units on both sides, so #{E} and its inverse
restrict to the stated actual groups. Applying the complex map to
#{svs^{-1}} and cancelling #{i} proves the action identity. This is the
sign-transfer mechanism used for compact forms in \ref{fcap-0039},
with the additional coordinate change #{T}.}

\p{The algebraic construction is also the composite of sign scaling
and the isometry #{T:(-Q_{1,3})\to Q_{3,1}}. TauCeti's general
scaling formula at the unit #{-1}
\leanref/tauceti{TauCeti.CliffordAlgebra.evenEquivEvenSMul_ι},
its reversion compatibility
\leanref/tauceti{TauCeti.CliffordAlgebra.evenEquivEvenSMul_reverseEven},
and the isometry formula
\leanref/tauceti{CliffordAlgebra.evenEquivOfIsometry_ι}
provide these three component statements. The displayed #{T} and its
Spin-action dictionary are the explicit specialization proved here.}

\p{Let #{\Phi:\Cl^+(Q_{3,1})\to M_2(\mathbb C)} be TauCeti's
concrete matrix equivalence. Its bilinear-generator formula
\leanref/tauceti{TauCeti.realCliffordThreeOneEvenEquivComplexMatrix_ι}
gives

##{\begin{aligned}
\Phi(f_0f_3)&=-\sigma_2,&\Phi(f_1f_3)&=\sigma_1,&
\Phi(f_2f_3)&=-\sigma_3,\\
\Phi(f_0f_1)&=i\sigma_3,&\Phi(f_0f_2)&=i\sigma_1,&
\Phi(f_1f_2)&=i\sigma_2.
\end{aligned}}

Since #{T(e_0)=f_3}, #{T(e_1)=f_1}, #{T(e_2)=-f_0}, and
#{T(e_3)=-f_2}, these formulas give #{\Phi(E(A_j))=\sigma_j}.
The #{A_j} generate the even algebra, hence #{\Phi\circ E=\Psi}.
Also #{E(e_0e_1e_2e_3)=f_0f_1f_2f_3}, whose matrix is #{-i1}.
Thus the Pauli group equivalence agrees, through #{E}, with
\leanref/tauceti{TauCeti.realSpinThreeOneEquivSpecialLinear}.
This dictionary concerns the even algebras and their Spin actions;
the full real Clifford algebras retain their different signature types.}

